// Body lowering: sema's typed tree to IR, one module's fn bodies at a time. The per-fn environment
// (locals, loop labels, defers) and the read-only program state every part sees.
//
// Port of: j3c/src/check/lower/mod.rs, check/lower/setup.rs,
// check/lower/defcheck.rs (replaced by sema typing generic bodies once with bound-only placeholders, B11.1),
// check/lower/lazy.rs (replaced by sema's instantiation queue, B11.2)
// J3: Lowering is a dumb walk (plan 11 B11.1): every type, method, trait impl and generic instance is already
//     chosen on sema's typed tree. Lower makes no type decisions and reports no type errors.
// J3: No `defcheck` (no `IrCx` clone, no throwaway lowering) and no `lazy_methods` + `wake` scan for `FnAddr`s:
//     generic fns, generic struct methods, vtables, bound checks and derives are instances sema requests on
//     one queue and drains to a fixed point before lowering (B11.2). Nothing unused is made, so nothing is
//     dropped after.
// J3: The unit of work is one module (B5): `lowerModule(&Session, module, sigs)` takes every signature as an
//     explicit input and reads no global state, so modules lower in parallel once signatures are done.
module j3c.lower;
